TEXT 80 32 Left 3 ;#215 A DC load on the output removes the notch
TEXT 80 88 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VgodYtiD_F0
TEXT 80 128 Left 2 ;The same follower and the same AC-coupled load, with Rdc added from the output to ground. The
TEXT 80 160 Left 2 ;op amp then sources current at all times, so the output stage never has to hand over.
TEXT 80 704 Left 2 !.include ..\..\LTspice\Models\onsemi\LM358_onsemi_2018.lib
TEXT 80 744 Left 2 !.tran 0 2m 1m 100n
TEXT 80 784 Left 2 !.four 5k V(ac_out)
TEXT 80 824 Left 2 !.meas tran vout_pp PP V(ac_out) FROM 1m TO 2m
TEXT 80 864 Left 2 !.meas tran iload_pp PP I(Rload) FROM 1m TO 2m
TEXT 80 904 Left 2 !.meas tran itotal_min MIN I(Rload)+I(Rdc) FROM 1m TO 2m
TEXT 80 968 Left 2 ;Alan's values throughout: 1 Vpp at 5 kHz, a 5 V supply, the 20k and 10k bias divider, 0.47 uF
TEXT 80 1000 Left 2 ;coupling capacitors and a 1 k load. The model is onsemi's LM358, which carries the class B
TEXT 80 1032 Left 2 ;output stage this lesson is about, so the notch comes from the model and is not drawn in.
